course: dictionary
lesson: 10927
title: Vomit and the words for being sick
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Vomit can be a verb or a noun. As a verb, it means to be sick: food and liquid come back up from your stomach and out of your mouth. As a noun, it is the food and liquid that comes out. Read the words around it to check which one you have.
explain: Many words mean the same thing in everyday talk. «Be sick» means vomit in British English, and «throw up» is the everyday word for it. «Chunder» is Australian slang, and «puke» is slang too. Use the sentence to decide which meaning fits.
explain: The context can also warn you. «You should not try to make someone vomit after swallowing a poison unless an expert tells you to.» The clue is the word poison, and the warning is that a strong chemical can burn the throat again on the way back up. So if someone has swallowed poison, get an adult or an expert to help straight away.
fact: Vomit can be a verb (to vomit) or a noun (the vomit).
fact: «Vomit» means to be sick, when food and liquid come back up from your stomach.
fact: «Be sick» in British English means vomit, not just feel ill.
fact: Children can pass on a tummy bug for about 48 hours after the last vomit or diarrhoea, so they stay off school for that long.
fact: If you vomit, tell an adult, wash your hands, sip small amounts of water, and stay home until you are better.
exercise: «Children can pass on a tummy bug for about 48 hours after the last vomit.» What does vomit mean here? | A type of sports game | *The food and liquid that comes out when you are sick | A kind of cold drink | Feeling very sleepy
exercise: Which phrase means the same as vomit? | Feel cold | Sleep in | Go to bed early | *Throw up
exercise: In first aid, a person who vomits and is very sleepy needs help. What should you do? | *Get an adult to help straight away | Give them a big meal | Let them sleep it off on their own | Laugh and walk away
test: «Be sick» in British English means what? | To feel very happy | To run fast | *To vomit | To sleep for a long time
test: Why should you not make someone vomit after swallowing poison unless an expert says so? | It makes them grow taller | *A strong chemical can burn the throat again on the way back up | It always cures poison | It tastes nice
exam: Which word is Australian slang for vomit? | Be sick | Puke | Throw up | *Chunder
